      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Jerome Catholic Church Picnic, called the Fancy Farm Picnic, began in 1881 as a local event that grew into a statewide political gathering.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancy_Farm%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1985, the Fancy Farm Picnic earned a Guinness World Record as the largest picnic, consuming 15,000 pounds of mutton, pork, and chicken.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancy_Farm%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Proceeds from the Fancy Farm Picnic fund the local Catholic elementary school and support community improvements.",
